  "description": "The proposal involves the replacement of the existing windows with new timber sash windows designed to replicate the original historic appearance of the property. The new units will match the existing window configurations, including glazing bar patterns, sash horns, frame proportions, and overall profiles, ensuring full visual continuity with the building’s historic character. All windows will be constructed in painted timber, consistent with the materials historically used in the Lee Green Conservation Area. While maintaining the original aesthetic, the new windows will incorporate improved thermal performance with double glazed to reduce heat loss and enhance the building’s energy efficiency. No alterations are proposed to the size of the openings or the surrounding fabric, and the works constitute a like‑for‑like replacement in appearance.",
